---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
const lang = 'en';
---

<DocsLayout lang={lang}>
  <h1 class="font-mono text-3xl font-bold text-mono-50">Runtime (roamyd)</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 text-mono-400 leading-relaxed">
    <code class="text-mono-200">roamyd</code> is the core daemon that manages terminal sessions. It listens for WebSocket connections, creates PTY-backed sessions, and streams terminal I/O to connected clients.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Architecture</h2>
  <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/50 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-mono-300"><code>              ┌─────────────────┐
  Clients ───WS──▶│    roamyd      │──PTY──▶ Shell / Programs
  (web/cli/       │  (session daemon) │
   mobile)        └────────┬─────────┘
                          │
                 ┌────────▼─────────┐
                 │  roamy-runtime    │
                 │  (core library)   │
                 │  - Session mgmt   │
                 │  - Persistence    │
                 │  - PTY abstraction│
                 └──────────────────┘</code></pre>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Workspace Crates</h2>
  <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-sm text-mono-400">
      <thead><tr class="border-b border-mono-800 text-left"><th class="pb-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-200">Crate</th><th class="pb-2 font-mono text-mono-200">Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-mono-800/50">
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>roamyd</code></td><td class="py-2">Runtime daemon &mdash; HTTP + WebSocket server, session lifecycle, protocol transport, TLS, auth</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>roamy-runtime</code></td><td class="py-2">Core library &mdash; session management, persistence, PTY abstraction (<code class="text-mono-200">PtyBackend</code> trait)</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>roamy-conpty</code></td><td class="py-2">Windows ConPTY integration (pseudo-terminal host backend)</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>roamy-pty-unix</code></td><td class="py-2">Unix PTY integration (openpty/forkpty backend)</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>roamy-cli</code></td><td class="py-2">Terminal session manager CLI (<code class="text-mono-200">roamy</code> command)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">CLI Flags</h2>
  <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/50 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-mono-300"><code>roamyd                # Start interactively (logs to terminal)
roamyd --daemon       # Fork into background (Unix only)
roamyd --no-tls       # Disable TLS (plain WebSocket)
roamyd --web-dir DIR  # Serve web assets from directory</code></pre>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Configuration</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    roamyd loads optional config from <code class="text-mono-200">~/.roamy/config.toml</code>. Environment variables always override file values.
  </p>
  <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/50 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-mono-300"><code># ~/.roamy/config.toml

[server]
host = "127.0.0.1"      # Bind address (env: ROAMY_HOST)
port = 9800              # Bind port (env: ROAMY_PORT)
shell = "/bin/bash"      # Default shell (env: ROAMY_SHELL)
data_dir = "~/.local/share/roamy/sessions"  # Session data (env: ROAMY_DATA_DIR)
web_dir = "/path/to/roamy-web/dist"  # Web assets (env: ROAMY_WEB_DIR)

[tls]
enabled = true           # Enable TLS (auto-generates self-signed cert)
cert_path = ""           # PEM certificate (optional)
key_path = ""            # PEM private key (optional)

[daemon]
idle_timeout_secs = 600  # Auto-exit when no active sessions</code></pre>

  <h3 class="mt-8 font-mono text-lg font-medium text-mono-100">Environment Variables</h3>
  <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-sm text-mono-400">
      <thead><tr class="border-b border-mono-800 text-left"><th class="pb-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-200">Variable</th><th class="pb-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-200">Default</th><th class="pb-2 font-mono text-mono-200">Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-mono-800/50">
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>ROAMY_HOST</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-6">127.0.0.1</td><td class="py-2">Bind address</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>ROAMY_PORT</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-6">9800</td><td class="py-2">Bind port</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>ROAMY_SHELL</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-6">pwsh.exe / /bin/sh</td><td class="py-2">Default shell</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>ROAMY_DATA_DIR</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-6">platform-specific</td><td class="py-2">Session persistence directory</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>ROAMY_CONFIG</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-6">~/.roamy/config.toml</td><td class="py-2">Config file path</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>ROAMY_TOKEN_FILE</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-6">~/.roamy/token</td><td class="py-2">Auth token file</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>ROAMY_IDLE_TIMEOUT</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-6">600</td><td class="py-2">Idle timeout in seconds</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>ROAMY_PID_FILE</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-6">platform-specific</td><td class="py-2">PID file path</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>ROAMY_SOCKET</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-6">platform-specific</td><td class="py-2">Unix domain socket path (Unix only)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">TLS</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    TLS is enabled by default using <code class="text-mono-200">rustls</code>. If no certificate is provided, roamyd auto-generates a self-signed certificate at startup. Provide your own cert/key via config or <code class="text-mono-200">--no-tls</code> to disable.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Authentication</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    Remote clients must authenticate via a device token. The token is generated on first run and stored at <code class="text-mono-200">~/.roamy/token</code> (SHA-256 hashed, 0600 permissions on Unix). When running interactively, the token is printed to stderr and embedded in the QR code for easy client pairing.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Session Persistence</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    Session metadata is persisted as JSON files (<code class="text-mono-200">&lt;session-id&gt;.json</code>) in the data directory. Each session also has a scrollback file (<code class="text-mono-200">&lt;session-id&gt;.scrollback</code>) that enables replay when a client reconnects. Scrollback is capped at 1 MB in memory with automatic trimming.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Daemon Mode (Unix)</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    On Unix systems, <code class="text-mono-200">roamyd --daemon</code> forks into background with <code class="text-mono-200">setsid</code>, redirects stdout/stderr to <code class="text-mono-200">~/.roamy/logs/roamyd.log</code>, and manages a PID file. Graceful shutdown via SIGTERM/SIGINT.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Shell Hook Injection</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    When the shell is detected as PowerShell (<code class="text-mono-200">pwsh</code> or <code class="text-mono-200">powershell</code>), roamyd automatically injects a startup hook that reports working directory changes and command lifecycle events. This enables features like the status bar showing the current directory.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
